course: dictionary
lesson: 7594
title: Words about people and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A priest is a person whose job is to lead religious services and look after people in a church or temple. The words around the word give clues. «The priest did not scold him for coming back.» Scold means to tell someone off, so this priest was kind and did not shout at him.
explain: Some priests also make special offerings or prayers for people. In a story, «Josh told it at confession, felt lighter afterwards, and then did what the priest asked» shows that the priest listened to Josh and gave him advice. Confession is when someone tells a priest what they did wrong.
explain: Other churches call their leader a minister, vicar or pastor. «Many Protestant and Anglican churches have women ministers and bishops; Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain (make into priests) only men; this is disputed.» Disputed means people argue about it. When you see a word like this, the text often explains it in brackets or with a clue.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Priest» means a person who leads religious services and looks after people in a church or temple.
fact: «Ordain» means to make someone into a priest or minister in a formal ceremony.
fact: «Confession» means telling a priest what you have done wrong, and saying sorry.
fact: «Disputed» means people argue about it and do not agree.
exercise: «The priest did not scold him for coming back.» What does scold mean? | Give a big present | *Tell someone off | Forget about | Sing a song to
exercise: In the story, «a priest and a Levite passed by on the other side». What did the priest do to the hurt man? | Paid for his care | Bandaged his wounds | Carried him home | *Walked past on the other side
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence «this is disputed». | this | is | sentence | *disputed
test: What does a priest do, according to the meaning? | Teaches only maths | Sells food in a shop | *Leads religious services and looks after people | Builds bridges and roads
test: Josh felt lighter after confession. What does confession mean? | A type of church bell | *Telling a priest what you did wrong | Singing loudly in a choir | Reading a long book
exam: Other churches call their leader a minister, vicar or pastor. Which word is another name for a church leader? | Confession | Ordain | Disputed | *Pastor
